# ── the chassis ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A third-party snapshot lives here during development. It is NOT redistributed
# from this repository: it has no asserted provenance yet (no upstream commit
# recorded), and vendoring is a deliberate act that happens once, through the
# upstream project's own documented vendor procedure, with the commit pinned and
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES carried forward complete. Until that is done, it stays out.
deepseek-harness-master/
vendor/

# ── internal working documents ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build notes, receipts and the internal spec. The public spec is SPEC.md.
internal/

# ── site material — never, under any circumstances ────────────────────────
# A completed patch layer encodes how one organisation actually works, and a
# tape is a record of real cases. Both belong to the site, in the site's own
# version control. Nothing of the kind is ever committed here.
*.patch.yml
!examples/worked/*.patch.yml
*.tape/
*.jsonl
# ...except the synthetic teaching tapes, which carry no real data and are
# checked by conformance/run.py to declare themselves synthetic.
!fixtures/tapes/*.jsonl

# ── the corpus ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pinned public sources are fetched, not redistributed: OPTN policy, the CFR
# text and CMS material belong to their publishers. The MANIFEST (hashes, URLs,
# accessed dates) and the citations ARE committed — they are what make every
# claim reproducible without this repository shipping somebody else's document.
corpus/*
!corpus/README.md
!corpus/MANIFEST.json
!corpus/citations.json

# ── derived corpus output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A chunker's output IS the source document, cut up. corpus/ is gitignored
# because OPTN policy, CFR text and state statutes belong to their publishers
# and this repository does not redistribute them — and a chunk of a pinned
# source is still that source. Smoke output, chunk directories, any derived
# extract: none of it is committed, wherever it lands.
#
# Learned on 2026-08-26: a `git add -A` swept 55 smoke-test chunks containing
# verbatim OPTN policy into a public commit. The gitignore covered corpus/ and
# nothing covered the DERIVATIVES.
**/_smoke/
**/_smoke2/
**/.chunks/
**/chunks_out/

# ── the percept stream ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated as the repository is used, and it records what a completion hit —
# gate refusals, expiries, derived deadlines. On a real site that is a trace of
# work against PHI-bearing material. The CODE is committed; the STREAM is not.
percepts/*.jsonl
registrar.state
registrar.heartbeat.json

# ── ordinary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.so
*.o
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
demo/_out/
